\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Example}
\title{Two opposite values over a ring}
\date{2026-11-17}

\p{Let #{C_2} exchange two points #{y_+,y_-} and act
on a #{k}-module #{E} by the scalar #{-1}.
For #{v\in E}, the [equivariant observable](fdip-00WK)
with values #{v,-v} and equal weight #{c} has sum
##{cv+c(-v)=0.}
This identity holds over every commutative ring.
Its partition coefficient is #{2c}, so a normalized
value exists only if #{2c} is a unit.
In characteristic two the sign action is trivial and
the two values are equal; their sum is still zero.}
